+- **What the tool verifies, and what it does not claim.** The tool verifies which exact plan was
+  executed: every result identifies, and the run verifies against the git object store, the plan
+  commit `F`, the pin table and configuration blobs, the tool commit `T` with every file it
+  executed, the evaluated commits and the producing CI run; the landing record that commits the
+  result is the result commit (sec. 5, 6.3). The owner confirms, procedurally and outside the
+  tool, that this was the approved plan. No output, outcome, field or control of the tool states
+  or implies that a plan, a record, a run or a result was approved or authorized. The retained
+  class names `authorized-replacement`, `authorized-removal`, `unauthorized-edit` and
+  `unauthorized-change` are identifiers carried from v1; they mean "specified by the frozen ledger"
+  and "not specified by it" and say nothing about owner approval.
+- **What v6.0 removes.** All automated verification of owner authorization: the tool authority
+  record `A` (schema `oi-tool-authority/2`); the versioned comment forms `oi-freeze/1`,
+  `oi-authority/1` and `oi-freeze-ledger/1`; "Owner at creation"; the freeze ledger; the reading of
+  any comment thread, comment edit history, hidden state or deletion event; the authority-change and
+  ledger-append procedures; the owner-authorization record `oi-owner-authorization/1` and its lint;
+  and every read of the host's GraphQL API and of its comment, Issue, pull-request, branch,
+  repository-history and file-content APIs. Nothing takes their place.
